Perfect — here’s your **full HTML form** updated with the revised “Approvals Before Launch” section written as **statements** (not questions) and now including the **LinkedIn access** field.  

You can copy and paste this directly into your CRM, website, or Google Form import tool — it’s fully formatted and matches your style.

---

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>FullyBooked CRM Setup Form</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #fafafa;
      color: #333;
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 40px auto;
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
    }
    h1, h2 {
      color: #4A7C6F;
    }
    label {
      font-weight: bold;
      display: block;
      margin-top: 18px;
    }
    input[type="text"],
    input[type="email"],
    input[type="url"],
    input[type="file"],
    textarea {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 10px;
      margin-top: 6px;
      border: 1px solid #ccc;
      border-radius: 6px;
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    textarea { resize: vertical; }
    .section {
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding-top: 10px;
      border-top: 2px solid #e0e0e0;
    }
    .submit-btn {
      margin-top: 30px;
      padding: 12px 24px;
      background-color: #4A7C6F;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 8px;
      font-size: 16px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .submit-btn:hover {
      background-color: #3a6158;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>FullyBooked CRM Setup Form</h1>
  <p>Hi there! Please fill this out so I can set up your CRM, outreach systems, and automations correctly. — Bethany 💻✨</p>

  <form action="#" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data">

    <!-- CRM / FullyBooked Setup -->
    <div class="section">
      <h2>CRM / FullyBooked Setup</h2>

      <label>Business name:</label>
      <input type="text" name="business_name" required>

      <label>Upload your logo:</label>
      <input type="file" name="logo">

      <label>Main contact email:</label>
      <input type="email" name="main_email" required>

      <label>Main contact phone number:</label>
      <input type="text" name="main_phone">

      <label>List of staff who should have CRM access (name + email):</label>
      <textarea name="staff_access" rows="3"></textarea>

      <label>Preferred booking link (Calendly, Acuity, Zoom, or other):</label>
      <input type="url" name="booking_link">

      <label>Are you okay with me setting this up in my FullyBooked CRM system for this phase?</label>
      <input type="text" name="crm_approval">
    </div>

    <!-- Domain + Email Warm-up -->
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Domain + Email Warm-up</h2>

      <label>Do you already have a domain to use for outreach?</label>
      <input type="text" name="existing_domain">

      <label>If not, are you okay with me purchasing one and handling setup?</label>
      <input type="text" name="domain_purchase_approval">

      <label>Login details or DNS access (SPF, DKIM, DMARC):</label>
      <textarea name="dns_access" rows="3"></textarea>

      <label>Preferred sender name (e.g., “Aesthetic Injector Academy Partnerships”):</label>
      <input type="text" name="sender_name">
    </div>

    <!-- Outreach & Target List -->
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Outreach & Target List</h2>

      <label>Who do you want to target (clinics, trainers, distributors, etc.)?</label>
      <textarea name="target_audience" rows="3"></textarea>

      <label>Sample of 5–10 ideal partners (so tone can match real people):</label>
      <textarea name="sample_partners" rows="3"></textarea>

      <label>Any existing lists (Apollo, events, CRM, etc.):</label>
      <textarea name="existing_lists" rows="3"></textarea>

      <label>Do I have your approval to pull a fresh Apollo list if needed?</label>
      <input type="text" name="apollo_approval">
    </div>

    <!-- Messaging & Offer -->
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Messaging & Offer</h2>

      <label>One-line course or offer summary:</label>
      <textarea name="offer_summary" rows="2"></textarea>

      <label>Main benefit or unique value you want mentioned:</label>
      <textarea name="key_benefit" rows="2"></textarea>

      <label>Price point or partnership structure (rev-share, wholesale, etc.):</label>
      <input type="text" name="price_structure">

      <label>Link to existing sales page or info deck:</label>
      <input type="url" name="sales_link">
    </div>

    <!-- Approvals Before Launch -->
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Approvals Before Launch</h2>

      <p>Before we go live, please review and confirm the following:</p>

      <label>Once I draft them, you’ll confirm that your outreach domain and sender emails look good.</label>
      <input type="text" name="domain_approval">

      <label>You’ll review and approve the AI SDR intro and follow-up templates before launch.</label>
      <input type="text" name="ai_sdr_approval">

      <label>You’ll approve the LinkedIn message copy once it’s ready.</label>
      <input type="text" name="linkedin_copy_approval">

      <label>You’ll review and approve the CRM stages and automation triggers so I can finalize setup.</label>
      <input type="text" name="crm_triggers_approval">

      <label>You’ll provide LinkedIn profile access (or admin/manager permissions) so I can connect and automate outreach campaigns through your account.</label>
      <input type="text" name="linkedin_access">
    </div>

    <!-- Nice-to-Haves -->
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Nice-to-Haves</h2>

      <label>Upload your headshot for personalization:</label>
      <input type="file" name="headshot">

      <label>Short bio for outreach personalization:</label>
      <textarea name="bio" rows="3"></textarea>

      <label>Testimonials or proof pieces (quotes, screenshots, etc.):</label>
      <textarea name="testimonials" rows="3"></textarea>

      <label>Social proof links (press, podcast, awards, etc.):</label>
      <textarea name="social_links" rows="3"></textarea>
    </div>

    <button class="submit-btn" type="submit">
